From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:38:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 118/159] backlight: qcom-wled: Add CABC minimum brightness

With qcom,cabc-sel set, the WLED follows the panel's content-adaptive
backlight control (CABC) signal and dims the LEDs on dark content. At
low brightness the dimming is visible as a flicker of the whole screen
when content changes, and there is little power left to save; vendor
kernels switch CABC off below a brightness threshold (Motorola:
mmi,low-bl-threshold).

Add an optional qcom,cabc-min-brightness property for WLED5: below
that brightness the CABC input is disabled, at or above it the
configured CABC signal is followed again. Without the property the
behaviour is unchanged.

On the Moto G 5G Plus, CABC lowers the backlight current by about
51 mA on a mostly dark screen.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c b/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
index 19fc631bfc52..303dc65641a3 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
@@ -197,6 +197,8 @@ struct wled {
 	bool disabled_by_short;
 	bool has_short_detect;
 	bool cabc_disabled;
+	u32 cabc_min_brightness;
+	bool cabc_low;
 	int short_irq;
 	int ovp_irq;
 
@@ -473,6 +475,8 @@ static int wled5_ovp_delay(struct wled *wled)
 	return delay_us;
 }
 
+static int wled5_cabc_config(struct wled *wled, bool enable);
+
 static int wled_update_status(struct backlight_device *bl)
 {
 	struct wled *wled = bl_get_data(bl);
@@ -481,6 +485,19 @@ static int wled_update_status(struct backlight_device *bl)
 
 	mutex_lock(&wled->lock);
 	if (brightness) {
+		/*
+		 * Content-adaptive dimming is distracting at low brightness:
+		 * follow the panel's CABC signal only above the threshold.
+		 */
+		if (wled->version == 5 && wled->cfg.cabc_sel &&
+		    wled->cabc_min_brightness &&
+		    wled->cabc_low != (brightness < wled->cabc_min_brightness)) {
+			wled->cabc_low = brightness < wled->cabc_min_brightness;
+			rc = wled5_cabc_config(wled, !wled->cabc_low);
+			if (rc < 0)
+				goto unlock_mutex;
+		}
+
 		rc = wled->wled_set_brightness(wled, brightness);
 		if (rc < 0) {
 			dev_err(wled->dev, "wled failed to set brightness rc:%d\n",
@@ -1745,6 +1762,9 @@ static int wled_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (rc)
 		return rc;
 
+	device_property_read_u32(&pdev->dev, "qcom,cabc-min-brightness",
+				 &wled->cabc_min_brightness);
+
 	val = WLED3_SINK_REG_BRIGHT_MAX;
 	of_property_read_u32(pdev->dev.of_node, "max-brightness", &val);
 	wled->max_brightness = val;
